<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Les Cayes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Les Cayes is a port city on the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, capital of the Sud <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. In the colonial and revolutionary periods it was the main town of the southern peninsula and the stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andre-rigaud">André Rigaud</a>, who based his separate southern government there in 1810–1811. In 1816 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> sailed from Les Cayes with Haitian help to renew the struggle for Venezuelan independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/les-cayes.jpg" alt="Les Cayes" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_Les_Cayes_Haiti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
